Professional Services Agreement between the Cheyenne Metropolitan Planning Organization
and Kimley-Horn and Associates for the Cheyenne Downtown Strategic Parking Plan (MPO
Planning Funds).  Reporting for Finance Committee, Mr. Brown moved to approve, seconded by Mr.
Luna.  Upon inquiry, Sreyoshi Chakraborti, Metropolitan Planning Office, provided information
relative to public engagement assistance; target audience and scope of work to be provided;
estimated time lines for the project and the study area, which will be the downtown core area, and
noted the last downtown parking study was conducted in 1991.  Discussion included possible
parking permits for residents in the downtown area; definition of the term “default”; MPO staff
project monitoring, and resulting consultant recommendations that may involve short and long term
implementation time frames.  Upon inquiry, Dan White, City Attorney, explained the definition of
“default” in relation to notice and remedy language contained in the agreement.  Motion carried
(amount not to exceed $85,535.00).  Voting “yes” all members of the governing body with the
exception of Ms. Williams voting “no”. (#6493)
